1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:03,600
In the deepest part of the ocean,
there is no light.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:04,900
None.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:09,600
Not a single photon from
the sun has ever reached this far.

4
00:00:10,133 --> 00:00:14,000
So where is that glow coming from?

5
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:18,800
Below 200m.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:19,600
Sunlight.

7
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,600
Disappears completely below 1000m.

8
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:25,900
It has never existed.

9
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:30,300
The deep ocean covers
more than half the surface of our planet.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,633
And remarkably,
nearly three quarters of everything

11
00:00:33,633 --> 00:00:36,733
that lives there produces its own light.

12
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,000
We think of the deep ocean as empty,

13
00:00:40,266 --> 00:00:43,266
silent, dead.

14
00:00:43,533 --> 00:00:46,500
What science has only recently confirmed
is that it

15
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:51,733
may be the most illuminated
environment on Earth, just not by the sun.

16
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:58,000
Every flash you see in these
waters is alive and it is doing something.

17
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,400
The mechanism is called bioluminescence,
and the chemistry behind

18
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:06,333
it sounds less like biology
and more like alchemy.

19
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:12,533
Every bioluminescent organism on Earth
uses a reaction between two molecules,

20
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:18,000
a protein called luciferase,
and a compound called luciferin.

21
00:01:18,866 --> 00:01:21,266
When oxygen is introduced, the reaction

22
00:01:21,266 --> 00:01:24,700
releases energy, not as heat as light.

23
00:01:24,733 --> 00:01:26,233
Cold light.

24
00:01:26,233 --> 00:01:30,300
Pure light with almost zero energy wasted.

25
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:34,133
It is, by every engineering
standard, more efficient

26
00:01:34,133 --> 00:01:37,466
than any light source
humans have ever built.

27
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:42,100
What makes this more remarkable
is what evolution did with it.

28
00:01:42,133 --> 00:01:45,433
Bioluminescence did not appear once

29
00:01:45,433 --> 00:01:48,433
spread across the tree of life
and diversify.

30
00:01:48,466 --> 00:01:51,666
It evolved independently in completely

31
00:01:51,666 --> 00:01:55,833
unrelated lineages
more than 40 separate times.

32
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:58,833
Fish that share no ancestor with squid.

33
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:01,600
Jellyfish with no connection to fungi.

34
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:04,600
Beetles with no relationship to bacteria.

35
00:02:04,866 --> 00:02:07,666
Each one arrived at the same solution.

36
00:02:07,666 --> 00:02:09,333
The same chemistry.

37
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:11,533
The same cold light.

38
00:02:11,533 --> 00:02:14,633
Evolution apparently has a favorite trick.

39
00:02:14,666 --> 00:02:18,300
The anglerfish is
perhaps the most famous example.

40
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:21,500
That glow is called the esca,

41
00:02:21,833 --> 00:02:24,900
a modified spine on the top of its head.

42
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:28,100
But here is what's extraordinary about it.

43
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:33,333
The anglerfish did not evolve the ability
to produce that light itself.

44
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:37,666
The esca glows
because it is filled with living bacteria,

45
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:43,533
bioluminescent microbes that colonize the
lure during the fish's early development.

46
00:02:43,833 --> 00:02:47,000
The fish and the bacteria exist
in a relationship

47
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,600
so precise that neither can survive
without the other,

48
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:56,233
and the angler fish controls the light,
dimming it, brightening

49
00:02:56,233 --> 00:03:01,933
it, pulsing it in rhythms to attract
specific prey at specific depths.

50
00:03:02,066 --> 00:03:03,600
It does not hunt.

51
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:07,700
It waits, and the light does the work.

52
00:03:07,866 --> 00:03:12,100
But not all
bioluminescence is designed to attract.

53
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:15,100
Some of it is designed to vanish.

54
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:19,400
The Hawaiian bobtail
squid lives in shallow coastal water,

55
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:23,900
where moonlight creates
a faint glow on the ocean surface.

56
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,700
Any creature swimming below
it would cast a shadow,

57
00:03:27,933 --> 00:03:32,100
a silhouette visible to predators
looking up.

58
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:37,500
So the squid solved this problem
with an organ on its underside,

59
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:42,200
filled with bioluminescent
bacteria, calibrated every night

60
00:03:42,233 --> 00:03:46,433
to match the exact brightness
and color of the moon above.

61
00:03:46,933 --> 00:03:49,700
No shadow, no silhouette.

62
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:52,700
The squid effectively disappears.

63
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:56,533
This technique is called
counter illumination,

64
00:03:56,533 --> 00:04:02,300
and it has evolved independently
in at least a dozen separate lineages.

65
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:05,466
Counter illumination is defensive.

66
00:04:05,466 --> 00:04:09,433
What comes next is not deep
in the midnight

67
00:04:09,466 --> 00:04:12,933
zone lives an animal called
the dragon fish.

68
00:04:13,333 --> 00:04:17,000
It has evolved something that,
until recently, scientists

69
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,833
believed was physically impossible
for biological tissue.

70
00:04:21,066 --> 00:04:26,266
The dragon fish can produce
and see red light.

71
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:28,733
This matters because red light

72
00:04:28,733 --> 00:04:32,300
does not penetrate below
a few hundred meters of ocean.

73
00:04:32,633 --> 00:04:35,700
Every other creature in the deep,
every predator,

74
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:39,500
every prey is effectively blind to it.

75
00:04:40,033 --> 00:04:43,000
The dragon fish moves
through a frequency of light

76
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,333
that no other animal
in that environment can perceive.

77
00:04:46,666 --> 00:04:50,833
It is hunting with a flashlight
that its prey cannot see.

78
00:04:50,866 --> 00:04:53,900
It is not alone in weaponizing light.

79
00:04:54,066 --> 00:04:59,466
The firefly squid coordinates
thousands of photophores across its body,

80
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:04,700
not to hide, but to create patterns
that disorient and confuse prey.

81
00:05:05,033 --> 00:05:07,833
The siphon offer a colonial organism

82
00:05:07,833 --> 00:05:11,133
that can reach 40m in length, pulses

83
00:05:11,133 --> 00:05:14,466
cascading waves of bioluminescence

84
00:05:14,466 --> 00:05:18,066
along its body to herd prey into range.

85
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:22,100
And some species of deep sea jellyfish,
when threatened,

86
00:05:22,133 --> 00:05:25,133
release glowing particles into the water.

87
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:29,000
A decoy cloud of light
that attracts a predators.

88
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,500
Predators.

89
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:33,066
They use light the way other animals

90
00:05:33,066 --> 00:05:37,666
use sound, smell, or venom as a tool.

91
00:05:37,833 --> 00:05:39,866
As a weapon.

92
00:05:39,866 --> 00:05:43,933
Evolution invented this solution
more than 40 times

93
00:05:43,966 --> 00:05:47,066
in fish, in squid, in fungi,

94
00:05:47,133 --> 00:05:50,366
in bacteria, in worms, in beetles.

95
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:56,133
Each time arriving at the same chemistry,
the same reaction, the same cold light.

96
00:05:56,433 --> 00:06:01,066
There is a principle in biology
called convergent evolution.

97
00:06:01,233 --> 00:06:05,133
When unrelated species
independently developed the same solution

98
00:06:05,133 --> 00:06:08,500
to the same problem, wings evolved

99
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:11,933
four times, eyes evolved 40 times.

100
00:06:11,933 --> 00:06:15,866
Bioluminescence
evolved more than 40 times.

101
00:06:15,866 --> 00:06:17,600
What that tells us is this.

102
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:22,333
Wherever life encounters darkness,
it finds a way to make light,

103
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:25,000
not just on Earth.

104
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:30,033
The deep ocean is the closest environment
we have to the conditions of Europa.

105
00:06:30,266 --> 00:06:34,866
Jupiter's moon with a liquid ocean
beneath miles of ice.

106
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:38,700
If life exists there, science now believes

107
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:43,266
it is almost certainly bioluminescent
in the dark.

108
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:45,266
Life lights itself.

109
00:06:45,266 --> 00:06:47,600
It has no other choice.
